-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
--  Auth users are NOT created here.
--
--  Supabase Auth owns `auth.users`, and inserting into it from SQL is brittle.
--  Create the accounts through the Admin API instead — from the server folder:
--
--      npm run provision
--
--  That script creates one auth user per row below, with the matching role and
--  branch metadata, which the `on_auth_user_created` trigger mirrors into
--  public.profiles. The three accounts you sign in with are:
--
--      manager@southwind.com.ph      management   (BR-QC)
--      warehouse@southwind.com.ph    warehouse    (BR-QC)
--      sales@southwind.com.ph        sales        (BR-QC)
--
--  The full roster the provisioner will create:
--      m.reyes@southwind.com.ph           management (BR-QC)
--      l.aquino@southwind.com.ph          management (BR-QC)
--      e.felipe@southwind.com.ph          management (BR-QC)
--      j.garcia@southwind.com.ph          management (BR-BW)
--      r.cruz@southwind.com.ph            management (BR-NZ)
--      r.villanueva@southwind.com.ph      management (BR-LG)
--      c.delacruz@southwind.com.ph        management (BR-IL)
--      a.santos@southwind.com.ph          management (BR-CB)
--      ma.santos@southwind.com.ph         management (BR-DP)
--      e.bautista@southwind.com.ph        management (BR-CDO)
--      j.marteja@southwind.com.ph         warehouse  (BR-QC)
--      k.catalan@southwind.com.ph         warehouse  (BR-CB)
--      g.limco@southwind.com.ph           warehouse  (BR-IL)
--      d.ocampo@southwind.com.ph          warehouse  (BR-BW)
--      m.cruz@southwind.com.ph            sales      (BR-QC)
--      n.bautista@southwind.com.ph        sales      (BR-DP)
